From: Devin kernel lane <kernel@rabbizos>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026
Subject: [PATCH] a21s: add PSCI cpu-sleep idle-state to all cpus

!!! DO NOT FLASH WITHOUT THE COMPANION KERNEL QUIRK !!!

Adds a "cpu-sleep" idle-state (arm,idle-state + arm,psci-suspend-param)
and wires cpu-idle-states on all 8 cpus (cpucl0 0x0-0x3, cpucl1
0x100-0x103). Param <0x10000> = affinity-level-1 (cluster) power down,
matching the convention used by exynos2200/gs101 dtsi.

KNOWN BLOCKER (findings a21s-modem-power-findings.md 5.3): the vendor
secure firmware on SM-A217F has "messed up MPIDRs" — Alexey Klimov's
working cpuidle patches exist but are not upstreamable and not public:
"needs some argument shift in one of the PSCI calls" (linux-arm-kernel,
Aug 2026). Flashing this DTS alone means the kernel will issue
CPU_SUSPEND with a *standard* MPIDR to firmware that expects a shifted
one — outcome untested on this device (likely NOT_SUPPORTED, possibly
suspending the wrong CPU). Only flash together with the MPIDR-shift
quirk or after a successful on-device CPU_SUSPEND probe.

cpuidle-psci requires arm,psci-suspend-param (states without it are
skipped), so the WFI-only fallback needs no DT change — architectural
WFI already works today.

Lane: kernel. Device: samsung/a21s.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos850-a217f.dts | 31 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos850-a217f.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos850-a217f.dts
@@ -1457,12 +1457,34 @@
 	};
 };
 
-/* ---- cpuidle hooks -------------------------------------------------
- * Vendor/PSCI cpuidle needs the exynos850-pmu patch series + PSCI
- * MPIDR workaround (findings 5.3). Cooling cells added now so thermal
- * cooling-maps can bind later; harmless without idle-states. */
-&cpu0 { #cooling-cells = <2>; };
-&cpu4 { #cooling-cells = <2>; };
+/* ---- cpuidle -------------------------------------------------------
+ * PSCI cpuidle on A21s is BLOCKED on a kernel-side quirk: vendor
+ * firmware has broken MPIDRs and needs a shifted CPU_SUSPEND argument
+ * (Klimov, linux-arm-kernel Aug 2026; patch not public). The states
+ * below are the correct DT description but MUST NOT be booted without
+ * that workaround - see patch header. */
+&cpus {
+	idle-states {
+		cpu_sleep: cpu-sleep {
+			compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+			idle-state-name = "cpu-sleep";
+			arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x10000>;
+			local-timer-stop;
+			entry-latency-us = <200>;
+			exit-latency-us = <250>;
+			min-residency-us = <1000>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&cpu0 { #cooling-cells = <2>; cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>; };
+&cpu1 { cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>; };
+&cpu2 { cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>; };
+&cpu3 { cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>; };
+&cpu4 { #cooling-cells = <2>; cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>; };
+&cpu5 { cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>; };
+&cpu6 { cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>; };
+&cpu7 { cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>; };
 
